 Let me grep for an existing test that asserts ErrCommandObjectSkipped.\n\nLet me search in tests for \"ErrCommandObjectSkipped\".\n\nLet me also look at the gitrestclient.GitClient interface to understand ListFiles/ReadFile, and the metrics interface for FrontmatterCommandsTotal.\n\nLet me also check the \"not_found counter increments\" — the executor increments m.FrontmatterCommandsTotal(operation, \"not_found\").Inc() when not found. The skip should not increment this. How to test zero increments? The tests use metrics.New() which is a real metrics object with prometheus counters. I can use testutil.ToFloat64 to check the counter value before/after. Let me look at how planning_retry_test.go does it — it uses `testutil.ToFloat64(metrics.PlanningRetryTotal.WithLabelValues(\"retry\"))`. Similarly I can use `metrics.FrontmatterCommandsTotal.WithLabelValues(\"update-frontmatter\", \"not_found\")`. Let me check the metrics package to see the exported collectors.\n\nLet me read metrics.go.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d516ec6-9c37-415d-ba1d-85d6d6e1eaa0","uuid":"9a6444a6-92a7-4ff9-970d-c825414bbd21","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:46:31.012Z"}
