{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_7307ac048ed24a0eaf97852b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now let me add the tests. Let me add a `Context(\"vault routing (frontmatter command)\")` block to each executor test.\n\nFor the update-frontmatter executor test, I'll add after the existing contexts, before the closing `})` of `Describe(\"HandleCommand\", ...)`. Actually, let me place it as a new top-level `Describe` or within `HandleCommand`. Let me look at the structure again — the test file ends with:\n\n```go\n\t\tContext(\"spec 042: prod incident reproducer (phase: human_review + Body Verdict section)\", func() {\n\t\t\t...\n\t\t})\n\t})  // end Describe HandleCommand\n})  // end Describe NewUpdateFrontmatterExecutor\n```\n\nI'll add a new `Context(\"vault routing\", ...)` inside `Describe(\"HandleCommand\", ...)` before its closing. Let me write it.\n\nFor the update executor:\n\n```go\nContext(\"vault routing\", func() {\n    It(\"skips a mismatched-vault command with zero git writes and zero not_found increments\", func() {\n        writeTaskFile(\n            \"task.md\",\n            \"---\\ntask_identifier: cross-vault-uuid\\nstatus: in_progress\\nphase: ai_review\\n---\\nbody\\n\",\n        )\n        cmd := buildCmdObj(task.UpdateFrontmatterCommand{\n            TaskIdentifier: lib.TaskIdentifier(\"cross-vault-uuid\"),\n            TargetVault:    \"personal\",\n            Updates:        lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"phase\": \"done\"},\n        })\n        _, _, err := executor.HandleCommand(ctx, nil, cmd)\n        Expect(errors.Is(err, cdb.ErrCommandObjectSkipped)).To(BeTrue())\n        Expect(fakeGit.AtomicReadModifyWriteAndCommitPushCallCount()).To(Equal(0))\n        Expect(fakeGit.ListFilesCallCount()).To(Equal(0))\n        Expect(testutil.ToFloat64(metrics.FrontmatterCommandsTotal.WithLabelValues(\"update-frontmatter\", \"not_found\"))).To(Equal(0.0))\n        // file untouched\n        fm := parseFrontmatter(taskFile)\n        Expect(fm[\"phase\"]).To(Equal(\"ai_review\"))\n    })\n\n    It(\"processes an empty-vault command (legacy fall-through)\", func() {\n        taskFile := writeTaskFile(\n            \"task.md\",\n            \"---\\ntask_identifier: legacy-uuid\\nstatus: in_progress\\nphase: ai_review\\n---\\nbody\\n\",\n        )\n        cmd := buildCmdObj(task.UpdateFrontmatterCommand{\n            TaskIdentifier: lib.TaskIdentifier(\"legacy-uuid\"),\n            Updates:        lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"phase\": \"done\"},\n        })\n        _, _, err := executor.HandleCommand(ctx, nil, cmd)\n        Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n        Expect(fakeGit.AtomicReadModifyWriteAndCommitPushCallCount()).To(Equal(1))\n        fm := parseFrontmatter(taskFile)\n        Expect(fm[\"phase\"]).To(Equal(\"done\"))\n    })\n\n    It(\"heals a file lacking target_vault, stamping the controller vault in the same write\", func() {\n        taskFile := writeTaskFile(\n            \"task.md\",\n            \"---\\ntask_identifier: heal-uuid\\nstatus: in_progress\\nphase: ai_review\\n---\\nbody\\n\",\n        )\n        cmd := buildCmdObj(task.UpdateFrontmatterCommand{\n            TaskIdentifier: lib.TaskIdentifier(\"heal-uuid\"),\n            Updates:        lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"phase\": \"done\"},\n        })\n        _, _, err := executor.HandleCommand(ctx, nil, cmd)\n        Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n        fm := parseFrontmatter(taskFile)\n        Expect(fm[\"target_vault\"]).To(Equal(\"openclaw\"))\n        // read back through ShouldProcessResult → false for a different vault\n        req := lib.Task{TaskIdentifier: lib.TaskIdentifier(\"heal-uuid\"), Frontmatter: lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"target_vault\": \"openclaw\"}}\n        Expect(routing.ShouldProcessResult(req, \"personal\")).To(BeFalse())\n        Expect(routing.ShouldProcessResult(req, \"openclaw\")).To(BeTrue())\n    })\n\n    It(\"never overrides an existing target_vault\", func() {\n        taskFile := writeTaskFile(\n            \"task.md\",\n            \"---\\ntask_identifier: stamped-uuid\\nstatus: in_progress\\nphase: ai_review\\ntarget_vault: personal\\n---\\nbody\\n\",\n        )\n        cmd := buildCmdObj(task.UpdateFrontmatterCommand{\n            TaskIdentifier: lib.TaskIdentifier(\"stamped-uuid\"),\n            Updates:        lib.TaskFrontmatter{\"phase\": \"done\"},\n        })\n        _, _, err := executor.HandleCommand(ctx, nil, cmd)\n        Expect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n        fm := parseFrontmatter(taskFile)\n        Expect(fm[\"target_vault\"]).To(Equal(\"personal\"))\n    })\n})\n```\n\nWait — but the executor is constructed with vaultName \"openclaw\". If a file has target_vault: personal and we're running as openclaw... hold on. The update command has empty TargetVault (legacy fall-through), so it processes. The file on disk has target_vault: personal. Heal only stamps when absent, so personal survives. Good — that tests (c).\n\nBut wait — there's a subtlety about the heal + routing interplay in test (c). The command has empty TargetVault so it processes (fall-through). The on-disk file has target_vault: personal. The heal should NOT override it. Correct.\n\nNow, for the imports, I need `errors`, `testutil`, `metrics`, `routing`. Let me check what's already imported in task_update_frontmatter_executor_test.go:\n- context, os, path/filepath, strings\n- lib, task, base, cdb\n- ginkgo, gomega\n- yaml\n- mocks, command, metrics\n\nI need to add: `errors` (std), `testutil` (prometheus), `routing`.\n\nLet me write the tests for the update executor first.\n\nAlso for the \"skips\" test, I assert `fakeGit.ListFilesCallCount()` == 0 — meaning the guard fired before the task-file lookup. Good.\n\nNow, one concern: the `metrics` package uses `promauto` registered counters at package level. When tests call `testutil.ToFloat64(metrics.FrontmatterCommandsTotal.WithLabelValues(\"update-frontmatter\", \"not_found\"))`, it returns the value