{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_8058a8ddb2124c09a5539298","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No `ignore-comments` flag, so funlen counts all lines (including blank and comment lines? funlen by default counts lines including comments and blank lines unless ignore-comments is set). Actually funlen's default counts statements and lines; `ignore-comments: true` makes it ignore comment lines. Since it's not set, comment lines count.\n\nThe complete executor function is 82 lines — over the 80 limit. But wait — was it already over before my change? Let me check. Before my change the function was shorter. Let me count the pre-change length: my routing guard added lines 61-75 (14 lines + blank). So before: ~68 lines. After: 82. Now it exceeds.\n\nI need to shorten it. Options:\n1. Extract the routing guard into a small helper that returns the skip error — but the guard needs glog + specific error. \n2. Reduce comments in the closure (funlen counts comment lines).\n3. Restructure so the closure is shorter.\n\nThe cleanest approach that keeps behavior: extract a helper `skipFrontmatterCommandVaultMismatch` that does the routing check and returns the error. But the routing guard needs `cmd.TargetVault`, `vaultName`, the operation name, and TaskIdentifier. Let me think about a clean design.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The simplest fix that reduces lines: move the routing guard BEFORE the func literal — i.e., deserialize outside... no, deserialize happens inside the closure.\n\nAlternative: create a small private helper:\n\n```go\n// frontmatterCommandVaultMismatch returns a wrapped cdb.ErrCommandObjectSkipped\n// when the command's non-empty TargetVault differs from vaultName, logging a\n// single glog.V(2) line. Returns nil when the command is owned (or legacy\n// unstamped, which falls through).\nfunc frontmatterCommandVaultMismatch(\n\tctx context.Context,\n\toperation string,\n\ttargetVault string,\n\tvaultName string,\n\ttaskID lib.TaskIdentifier,\n) error {\n\tif routing.ShouldProcessFrontmatterCommand(targetVault, vaultName) {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tglog.V(2).Infof(\n\t\t\"%s: skipped vault mismatch target_vault=%q vault=%q task=%s\",\n\t\toperation, targetVault, vaultName, taskID,\n\t)\n\t// ErrCommandObjectSkipped — not nil: a nil return with SendResultEnabled\n\t// publishes a spurious Success event on the shared result topic for every\n\t// cross-vault frontmatter command.\n\treturn errors.Wrapf(ctx, cdb.ErrCommandObjectSkipped, \"cross-vault %s for task %s\", operation, taskID)\n}\n```\n\nThen in each executor:\n```go\nif err := frontmatterCommandVaultMismatch(ctx, \"update-frontmatter\", cmd.TargetVault, vaultName, cmd.TaskIdentifier); err != nil {\n    return nil, nil, err\n}\n```\n\nThis reduces each closure by ~13 lines. For the complete executor: 82 - 13 ≈ 69 lines. Under 80.\n\nBut wait — the helper is shared across three executors. Where should it live? It uses `routing`, `glog`, `errors`, `cdb`, `lib`. It could go in a shared file in pkg/command. Since all three executors are in pkg/command, I can add it to one of them or a new small file. The CLAUDE.md guidance says files > 2000 lines should be split. Let me put the helper in the update executor file, or better, create a small dedicated helper. Actually, the cleanest is to put it in `task_update_frontmatter_executor.go`... hmm, but it's used by all three. Let me create it in a neutral location. \n\nActually — the existing code has `parseTaskFrontmatter`, `intFromFrontmatter`, `marshalFileContent` in task_increment_frontmatter_executor.go, shared across executors. So there's precedent for shared helpers living in one executor file. I'll put `frontmatterCommandVaultMismatch` in the update executor file (or increment). Let me put it in the update executor file right after the NewUpdateFrontmatterExecutor function, since that's where the pattern starts.\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety with error message wording: the requirement says \"log the skip at glog.V(2) naming the command's target vault and VAULT_NAME\". My helper does that. The error wrap message should name the operation. Good.\n\nLet me refactor all three executors to use the helper. This also reduces duplication (single decision).\n\nLet me implement:\n\n1. Add `frontmatterCommandVaultMismatch` helper in task_update_frontmatter_executor.go.\n2. Replace the inline guard in update executor.\n3. Replace inline guard in increment executor.\n4. Replace inline guard in complete executor.\n\nThen re-measure function lengths.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d516ec6-9c37-415d-ba1d-85d6d6e1eaa0","uuid":"a74f91b7-f03a-4714-9a7f-4c10f4d26947","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:51:57.861Z"}
